# AN AllDisjointClasses WITH FEWER THAN TWO MEMBERS. OWL 2 requires at least
# two operands, so this is not a DisjointClasses axiom at all. Decoded as one,
# the single member became disjoint from itself - A unsatisfiable, a false
# INCOHERENT - and an empty member list became ⊤ ⊑ ⊥, a false INCONSISTENT.
# It is now recognized as malformed and omitted: the run is INCONCLUSIVE, and
# nothing is derived from it. (The OWL API reads it as an axiom anyway, so
# HermiT calls A unsatisfiable; this directory is not diffed against oracles.)
# Expect: INCONCLUSIVE, consistent, A satisfiable, 2 omissions, exit 2.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class .
[] a owl:AllDisjointClasses ; owl:members ( :A ) .
[] a owl:AllDisjointClasses ; owl:members () .
